hadiths[51]{hadithnumber,text}:
"22034","Surayj ibn al-Numan narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Said ibn Abi Hilal, from Umar al-Dimashqi, from Umm al-Darda, she said: Abu al-Darda narrated to me that he prostrated with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eleven prostrations, among them al-Najm."
"22035","Affan narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Dawud ibn Amr informed us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Zakariyya al-Khuzai, from Abi al-Darda, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will be called on the Day of Resurrection by your names and the names of your fathers, so make your names good."
"22036","Isam ibn Khalid narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Maryam al-Ghassani narrated to me, from Khalid ibn Muhammad al-Thaqafi, from Bilal ibn Abi al-Darda, from Abi al-Darda, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Your love for a thing blinds and deafens."
"22037","He said, and Abu al-Yaman narrated it to us, he did not raise it, and al-Qurqusani Muhammad ibn Musab raised it."
"22038","Isam ibn Khalid narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abdullah narrated to me, from Damra, from Abi al-Darda, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Part of the understanding of a man is his gentleness in his livelihood."
"22039","Abu al-Mughira narrated to us, Said ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ubaydullah narrated to me, from Umm al-Darda, from Abi al-Darda, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and one of us would place his hand upon his head from the severity of the heat, and none among us was fasting except the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abdullah ibn Rawaha."
"22040","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Thabit, or from Abi Thabit, that a man entered the mosque of Damascus and said: O Allah comfort my loneliness, and have mercy on my strangeness, and provide me a righteous companion, so Abu al-Darda heard him and said: If you are truthful then I am happier with what you said than you, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Among them is a wrongdoer to himself, meaning the wrongdoer is seized in that standing of his, so that is worry and grief, and among them is moderate, he said: He is reckoned an easy reckoning, and among them is a forerunner in good deeds by the permission of Allah, he said: Those who enter Paradise without reckoning."
"22041","Abu Amir narrated to us, Hisham, meaning Ibn Sad, narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Hayyan al-Dimashqi, Umm al-Darda informed me, from Abi al-Darda, he said: We saw ourselves with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in some of his journeys on the hot day of severe heat, until a man would place his hand upon his head in the severity of the heat, and there was none among the people fasting except the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abdullah ibn Rawaha."
"22042","Abu Muawiya narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan al-Qurdusi narrated to us, from Qays ibn Sad, from a man who narrated to him, from Abi al-Darda, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the giving of the ruler, he said: Whatever Allah gives you of it without asking nor aspiring, then take it and use it as wealth, he said, and al-Hasan, may Allah have mercy on him, said: There is no harm in it so long as you do not travel to it or aspire for it."
"22043","Abu Muawiya narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Salim, from Umm al-Darda, she said: Abu al-Darda entered upon her one day angry, so she said: What is wrong with you, he said: By Allah I do not recognize among them anything of the affair of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except that they pray together."
"22044","Ismail narrated to us, Hisham informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Yaish ibn al-Walid ibn Hisham, from Madan or Mudan, from Abi al-Darda, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) vomited then broke his fast, he said: So I met Thawban in the mosque of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about that, so he said: I poured the ablution water for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"22045","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Said, the freed slave of Ibn Ayyash narrated to me, from Abi Bahriyya, and my father narrated to us, Makki narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Said narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abi Bahriyya, from Abi al-Darda, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you of the best of your deeds, Makki said, and the purest of them with your King, and the highest of them in your ranks, and better for you than giving gold and silver, and better for you than meeting your enemy so you strike their necks and they strike your necks, they said: And what is that O Messenger of Allah, he said: The remembrance of Allah Almighty."
"22046","Yahya narrated to us, from Shuba, from Yazid ibn Khumayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from his father, from Abi al-Darda, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a pregnant woman near the door of a tent or the edge of a tent, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perhaps her owner has intercourse with her, they said: Yes, he said: I intended to curse him with a curse that would enter with him into his grave, how does he make him inherit while he is not lawful for him, and how does he use her as a servant while she is not lawful for him."
"22047","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Musa ibn Uqba narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to me a hadith raising it to Abi al-Darda, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Shall I not inform you of the best of your deeds, then he mentioned the hadith, meaning the hadith of Yahya ibn Said and Makki, from Abdullah ibn Said, from Ziyad ibn Abi Ziyad."
"22048","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Shuba, Qatada narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Madan, from Abi al-Darda, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Would one of you be pleased to recite a third of the Quran in a night, they said: How can he bear that, or who can bear that, he said: Say: He is Allah One."
"22049","Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, Suhayl ibn Abi Salih narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Yazid, he said: I asked Said ibn al-Musayyab about the hyena, so he disliked it, so I said to him: Your people eat it, he said: They do not know, then a man with him said: I heard Abu al-Darda narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he forbade every possessor of plunder, and every possessor of snatching, and every possessor of fang among predators, Said said: He spoke the truth."
"22050","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Ata, from Safwan ibn Abdullah ibn Safwan, he said, and under him was al-Darda, he said: I came to Syria and entered upon Abu al-Darda but did not find him, and found Umm al-Darda, so she said: Do you intend Hajj this year, he said, I said: Yes, so she said: Then supplicate for us with good, for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Indeed the supplication of the Muslim is answered for his brother in his absence, at his head is an entrusted angel, whenever he supplicates for his brother with good he says: Amen, and for you the like, so I went out to the market and met Abu al-Darda, so he said to me the like of that, tracing it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"22051","Yazid ibn Harun and Yala said: Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Abi al-Zubayr, from Safwan, Yazid said: Ibn Abdullah, then he mentioned it."
"22052","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Malik, meaning Ibn Mighwal, narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Abi Umar, from Abi al-Darda, he said: A man stayed with Abu al-Darda, so Abu al-Darda said: Resident so we let graze, or departing so we fodder, he said: Rather departing, he said: Then I will provision you with provision, had I found what is better than it I would have provisioned you, I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, the rich have taken the world and the Hereafter, we pray and they pray, and we fast and they fast, and they give charity and we do not give charity, he said: Shall I not guide you to a thing, if you do it none who was before you will precede you, and none after you will reach you, except one who does what you do: after every prayer thirty-three glorifications, and thirty-three praises, and thirty-four takbirs."
"22053","Waki narrated to us, Zaida ibn Qudama narrated to me, al-Saib ibn Hubaysh al-Kalai narrated to me, from Madan ibn Abi Talha al-Yamari, he said: Abu al-Darda said to me: Where is your dwelling, he said, I said: In a village below Hims, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There are no three in a village where the adhan is not called nor prayer established among them but Satan overcomes them, so upon you is the congregation, for the wolf eats the stray."
"22054","Abu Said also narrated to us, Zaida narrated to us, al-Saib ibn Hubaysh al-Kalai narrated to us, then he mentioned it."
"22055","Yazid narrated to us, Hammam ibn Yahya informed us, from Qatada, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Madan ibn Abi Talha, from Abi al-Darda, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever memorizes ten verses from the beginning of Surah al-Kahf is protected from the Dajjal."
"22056","Yazid narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn Artah narrated to us, from Ibn Numan, from Bilal ibn Abi al-Darda, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed two young fattened rams."
"22057","Surayj narrated to us, Abu Shihab narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from Yala ibn Numan, from Bilal ibn Abi al-Darda, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed two young castrated rams."
"22058","Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to us, Asim ibn Raja ibn Haywa informed us, from Kathir ibn Qays, he said: A man came from Madinah to Abu al-Darda while he was in Damascus, so he said: What brought you O my brother, he said: A hadith reached me that you narrate from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Did you not come for trade, he said: No, he said: Did you not come for a need, he said: No, he said: You came only seeking this hadith, he said: Yes, he said: Then I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever travels a path seeking in it knowledge, Allah takes him by a path to Paradise, and the angels lower their wings in pleasure for the seeker of knowledge, and those in the heavens and the earth seek forgiveness for the scholar, even the fish in the water, and the virtue of the scholar over the worshipper is like the virtue of the moon over the rest of the stars, indeed the scholars are the heirs of the prophets, they did not inherit a dinar nor a dirham, rather they inherited knowledge, so whoever takes it takes an ample share."
"22059","al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Asim ibn Raja ibn Haywa, from Dawud ibn Jamil, from Kathir ibn Qays, he said: A man came from Madinah, then he mentioned its meaning."
"22060","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, he said: I heard Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami narrating that a man whose mother ordered him, or his father, or both of them, Shuba said, he says that, to divorce his wife, so he imposed upon himself a hundred freed slaves, then he came to Abu al-Darda while he was praying Duha lengthening it, and prayed between Dhuhr and Asr, then he asked him, so Abu al-Darda said to him: Fulfill your vow and be dutiful to your parents, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The father is the middle gate of Paradise, so guard the father or leave."
"22061","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Ishaq narrating that he heard Abu Habiba saying: A man bequeathed dinars in the path of Allah, so Abu al-Darda was asked, then he narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: The example of one who frees or gives charity at his death is like the example of one who gives a gift after he is satiated, Abu Habiba said: Something of that befell me."
"22062","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abi Ishaq, from Abi Habiba al-Tai, he said: My brother entrusted to me a portion of his wealth, he said: So I met Abu al-Darda and said: My brother entrusted to me a portion of his wealth, so where shall I place it, among the poor, or among the mujahidin, or among the needy, he said: As for me, had I been I would not have preferred over the mujahidin, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The example of one who frees at death is like the example of one who gives a gift when satiated."
"22063","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Muawiya, meaning Ibn Salih, from Abi al-Zahiriyya, from Kathir ibn Murra, from Abi al-Darda, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, is there recitation in every prayer, he said: Yes, then a man from the Ansar said: This has become obligatory."
"22064","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Qatada, from Khulayd al-Asari, from Abi al-Darda, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No sun ever rose but two angels are sent at its sides calling, making the inhabitants of the earth hear except the thaqalayn: O people come to your Lord, for what is little and suffices is better than what is much and distracts, and no sun ever set but two angels are sent at its sides calling, making the inhabitants of the earth hear except the thaqalayn: O Allah give the spender replacement, and give the withholder destruction of wealth."
"22065","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, al-Faraj ibn Fadala narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Abi Halbas, from Umm al-Darda, from Abi al-Darda, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah finished for every servant of His creation five: his term, and his deed, and his resting place, and his trace, and his provision."
"22066","Zayd ibn Yahya al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Khalid ibn Subayh al-Murri judge of al-Balqa narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ubaydullah narrated to us, that he heard Umm al-Darda narrating from Abi al-Darda, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah finished for every servant five: his term, and his provision, and his trace, and whether wretched or happy."
"22067","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated to us, Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm narrated to us, that he visited Abu al-Darda in Hims and stayed with him nights, and he ordered his donkey to be saddled with a pack saddle, so Abu al-Darda said: I see myself only following you, so he ordered his donkey to be saddled, then they traveled together upon their donkeys, then they met a man who had attended Friday yesterday with Muawiya at al-Jabiya, so the man recognized them but they did not recognize him, then he informed them the news of the people, then the man said: And another news I disliked to inform you, I see you dislike it, so Abu al-Darda said: Perhaps Abu Dharr was exiled, he said: Yes by Allah, so Abu al-Darda and his companion said: Indeed to Allah we belong and to Him we return, nearly ten times, then Abu al-Darda said: Watch them and be patient as was said to the companions of the she-camel, O Allah if they belie Abu Dharr then I do not belie him, O Allah if they accuse him then I do not accuse him, O Allah if they deem him dishonest then I do not deem him dishonest, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to trust him when he trusted no one, and confide to him when he confided to no one, indeed by the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Abu al-Darda, had Abu Dharr cut my right hand I would not hate him after what I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: No green sky shaded, nor dusty earth carried, one with an accent more truthful than Abu Dharr."
"22068","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hamza narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, Zayd ibn Artah narrated to me, he said: I heard Jubayr ibn Nufayr narrating from Abi al-Darda, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The encampment of the Muslims on the day of the great battle is al-Ghuta, beside a city called Damascus."
"22069","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Ata, from Abi Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, he said: A man came to Abu al-Darda and said: My wife is the daughter of my uncle and I love her, and my mother orders me to divorce her, so he said: I do not order you to divorce her, nor do I order you to disobey your mother, but I narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The mother is the middle of the gates of Paradise, so if you wish keep, and if you wish leave."
"22070","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, Anas ibn Iyad al-Laythi Abu Damra narrated to me, from Musa ibn Uqba, from Ali ibn Abdullah al-Azdi, from Abi al-Darda, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah Almighty said: Then We gave the Book as inheritance to those We chose of Our servants, among them a wrongdoer to himself, and among them moderate, and among them a forerunner in good deeds by the permission of Allah, as for those who preceded in good deeds, then those are those who enter Paradise without reckoning, and as for those who were moderate, then those are reckoned an easy reckoning, and as for those who wronged themselves, then those are those who are detained in the length of the gathering, then they are those whom Allah reaches with His mercy, so they are those who say: Praise to Allah Who removed grief from us, indeed our Lord is Forgiving Thankful, up to His saying: toil."
"22071","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas al-Juhani, from his father, that he entered upon Abu al-Darda, so he said: With health not with sickness, so Abu al-Darda said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Headache and fever do not cease with the believer, though his sin is like Uhud, leaving nothing upon him of that like the weight of a mustard seed."
"22072","Makki ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Said narrated to us, from Harb ibn Qays, from Abi al-Darda, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever bathes on Friday, and wears his clothes, and touches perfume if he has it, then walks to Friday with tranquility, and does not step over anyone nor harm him, and bows what was decreed for him, then waits until the imam leaves, is forgiven what is between the two Fridays."
"22073","Makki narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Said narrated to us, from Harb ibn Qays, from Abi al-Darda, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat one day upon the minbar and addressed the people and recited a verse, and beside me was Ubayy ibn Kab, so I said to him: O Ubayy when was this verse sent down, he said: So he refused to speak to me, then I asked him and he refused to speak to me, until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) descended, so Ubayy said to me: You have of your Friday only what you engaged in idle talk, then when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left I came to him and informed him, so I said: O Messenger of Allah you recited a verse, and beside me was Ubayy ibn Kab, so I asked him when this verse was sent down, but he refused to speak to me, until when you descended Ubayy claimed that I have of my Friday only what I engaged in idle talk, so he said: Ubayy spoke the truth, so when you hear your imam speaking then be silent until he finishes."
"22074","Ibrahim ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, my father said, and Ali ibn Ishaq, Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak informed us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir narrated to us, Zayd ibn Artah narrated to me, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Abi al-Darda, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Seek for me your weak ones, for you are only provided and aided by your weak ones."
"22075","Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to us, Baqiyya informed us, from Habib ibn Umar al-Ansari, from a shaykh with the kunya Abu Abd al-Samad, he said: I heard Umm al-Darda saying: Abu al-Darda when he narrated a hadith would smile, so I said: People will say you are foolish, so he said: I never saw, or I never heard, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrating a hadith but he smiled."
"22076","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hamza narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Waqid, Busr ibn Ubaydullah narrated to me, Abu Idris al-Khawlani narrated to me, from Abi al-Darda, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: While I was sleeping I saw the pillar of the Book taken from under my head, so I thought it was taken away, so I followed it with my sight, then it was taken to Syria, indeed faith when tribulations occur is in Syria."
"22077","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban narrated to us, from Umayr ibn Hani, from Abi al-Adhra, from Abi al-Darda, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Revere Allah He will forgive you, Ibn Thawban said, meaning submit."
"22078","Yunus narrated to us, Baqiyya narrated to us, from Habib ibn Umar al-Ansari, from Abi Abd al-Samad, from Umm al-Darda, she said: Abu al-Darda would not narrate a hadith but he smiled in it, so I said to him: I fear people will deem you foolish, so he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not narrate a hadith but he smiled."
"22079","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, Zabban narrated to us, from Sahl ibn Muadh, from his father, from Abi al-Darda, that he came to him visiting, so Abu al-Darda said to the father after greeting him: With health not with pain, three times saying that, then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The Muslim man does not cease to be afflicted with fever and headache, though his sins are greater than Uhud, until it leaves him with no sins upon him like the weight of a mustard seed."
"22080","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr, from Abi al-Darda, he said: The Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am the first for whom permission is given for prostration on the Day of Resurrection, and I am the first for whom permission is given to raise his head, so I look before me and recognize my ummah among the nations, and behind me the like of that, and on my right the like of that, and on my left the like of that, so a man said to him: O Messenger of Allah how do you recognize your ummah among the nations between Nuh and your ummah, he said: They are bright with marks from the trace of ablution, none other than them is likewise, and I recognize them that they are given their books in their right hands, and I recognize them, their offspring hasten before them."
"22081","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he doubted in it, he said: I heard Abu Dharr or Abu al-Darda, Yahya says: So I recognize them that their light hastens before them and on their right."
"22082","Yamur narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Lahia narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, that he heard Abu Dharr or Abu al-Darda, both said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am the first for whom permission is given in prostration, then he mentioned its meaning."
"22083","Qutayba ibn Said narrated to us, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr, that he heard from Abu Dharr and Abu al-Darda, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I know my ummah on the Day of Resurrection among the nations, they said: O Messenger of Allah how do you recognize your ummah, he said: I recognize them, they are given their books in their right hands, and I recognize them by their mark in their faces from the trace of prostration, and I recognize them by their light hastening before them."
"22084","Abu al-Mughira narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Maryam al-Ghassani narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas Hakim ibn Umayr and Habib ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Abi al-Darda, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you leave working for Allah Almighty a thousand good deeds when he enters the morning, saying: Glory of Allah and with His praise a hundred times, for it is a thousand good deeds, for he will not do, Allah willing, the like of that in sins in a day, and what he does of good besides that will be abundant."
